{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre \"trial of louis\" \"republic\" \"die\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_745760649#0_831468607","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2585","rank":2,"snippet":": 1267.000000 , \"headings\": \"Maximilien Robespierre Maximilien Robespierre Contents Quotes Misc Quotes On the Silver Mark (1791) On Subsistence (2 December 1792) Speech on the <cover>Trial of Louis XVI (Dec. 3, 1792) Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen (1793) Speech to the National Convention (5 February 1794) \"On the Principles of Political Morality\" Principles to Form the Basis of the Administration of the Republic (February 1794) (full text online) Quotes about Robespierre External links \" , \"segment\": \"Maximilien Robespierre - Wikiquote [ hide] Your continued donations keep Wikiquote running! Maximilien Robespierre From Wikiquote Jump to navigation Jump to search The secret of freedom lies in educating people, whereas the secret of tyranny is in keeping them ignorant. Men of all countries are brothers, and the different peoples should help one another to the best of their ability, like citizens of the same state. I utter this deadly truth with regret, but Louis must die, </cover>because the homeland has to live. The most extravagant idea that can be born in the head of a political thinker is to believe that it suffices for people to enter, weapons in ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1394957137#2_1920030353","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
