{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1284741093#4_2098896924","relevance":3,"reason":"This segment directly quotes Robespierre at Louis XVI's trial: the issue was public safety and national foresight, Louis should perish rather than many virtuous citizens, and Louis must die so the country may live.","learned":"Robespierre justified killing the king as a public-safety measure: sacrificing Louis was necessary to save the country and prevent harm to virtuous citizens."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2590","reason":"The focused trial/'must die' query is still producing direct trial-speech evidence, so continue while it remains productive."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2590"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_1190253790#8_2684454064","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2590","rank":4,"snippet":" , \"headings\": \"FRENCH REVOLUTION OVERVIEW FRENCH REVOLUTION OVERVIEW\" , \"segment\": \"The revolutionaries forced Louis XVI and his family to return to Paris and removed the little remaining authority he still had. Louis XVI was, from that point on, viewed as a traitor to the revolution. The National Convention took over power from the Legislative Assembly and was much more radical in nature. As such, the National Convention moved quickly to put Louis XVI on <cover>trial. Louis XVI was charged with treason due to his attempt to flee the country and was convicted by the National Convention. The famous revolutionary, Maximilien Robespierre, commented that “Louis must die </cover>so the nation may live.” Louis’ punishment was death and on, January 21st, 1793, Louis VXI was beheaded by guillotine. Execution of Louis XVI Execution of Marie Antionette In the months that followed, the National Convention declared war against several European nations, including: Britain, the Dutch Republic and Spain. As well, the National Convention created the Committee of Public Safety in April of 1793, which was tasked with protecting the new French republic against foreign attack and internal revolts.\" , \"start_char"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"11/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_1190253790#8_2684454064","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly explains that Louis XVI was viewed as a traitor, charged with treason for trying to flee, and that Robespierre said 'Louis must die so the nation may live,' providing direct evidence of his rationale.","learned":"Robespierre's argument is again tied to Louis XVI's perceived treason and the survival/protection of the new French republic."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2590","reason":"This focused query is still returning direct evidence about the trial, treason charge, and Robespierre's 'Louis must die' rationale, so continue while productive."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2590"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_1283188868#5_2360938783","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2590","rank":6,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_1283188868#5_2360938783\" , \"end_char\": 4771.000000 , \"headings\": \"Off with their heads! 5 French Revolution executions that changed history Off with their heads! 5 French Revolution executions that changed history “Louis <cover>must die so that the nation may live.” Maximilien Robespierre King Louis XVI Marie Antoinette Jean Sylvain Bailly The Drownings at Nantes Maximilien Robespierre Follow us on Twitter and Facebook to get high on history \" , \"segment\": \"Robespierre once declared starkly that “terror is justice” but when he found himself on trial, </cover>he attempted suicide and shot himself in the head. The attempt failed and a hideously wounded Robespierre went to the guillotine on 28th July 1794. From monarchy to republic and beyond, the French Revolution was a time of enormous instability. As the guillotine blade fell and the Revolutionary Wars raged, a soldier began to make his mark on the battlefield, emerging to lead his country and become a military legend in his own right. That man’s name was Napoleon, but his is a story for another day. Glorious ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1394957137#2_1920030353","rank":5,"relevance":3}]}}
