{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_283399488#1_692564532","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage gives background on sans-culottes, Jacobins, and demands for a republic instead of monarchy, but it does not explain Robespierre's specific reason for wanting Louis XVI executed.","learned":"General 'execute the king' searches are retrieving broad radical/Jacobin background rather than direct evidence of Robespierre's rationale."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre \"trial\" \"louis capet\" \"republic\")","reason":"Search with Louis XVI's revolutionary name and trial/republic context to find focused sources on Robespierre's argument that Louis Capet's death was necessary for the republic."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre \"trial\" \"louis capet\" \"republic\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_728658300#4_752179745","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2615","rank":3,"snippet":"1789, was stylized in the 1880s, and was commercialized in the late Twentieth Century, when she became identified with the actress Brigitte Bardot. Still, as considerable historiography has shown, one should not assume that because a woman could becomes a powerful symbol of revolution that women obtained any significant political, social, or economic advantages during the French Revolution. As Joan Landes has argued, \"Marianne\" was nothing more than a picture; the new Republic was a discursive <cover>republic based on laws and texts, which emptied the symbol of any real political significance. ROBESPIERRE AND THE TERROR On June 20, 1791, after revolutionaries had turned parish priests into civil servants who had to swear allegiance to a secular, national, state, Louis Capet, King of France, fled Paris with his family, hoping to meet up with Austrian forces, which would help him restore the traditional monarchy. He was recognized and captured at Varennes, brought back to Paris, then executed after a trial </cover>on January 21, 1793.\" , \"start_char\": 4040.000000 , \"title\": \"The French Revolution\" , \"url\": \"http://faculty.fullerton.edu/nfitch/history110b/rev.html\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1394957137#2_1920030353","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1284741093#4_2098896924","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
