{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre \"louis xvi\" \"symbol of the old regime\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_1845745608#1_3163774589","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2619","rank":1,"snippet":"grant the reforms that were demanded and revolution followed. Louis and his queen, Marie Antoinette, were executed in 1793. The Third Estate 97% of pre-revolutionary France's population, this estate was comprised of workers, peasants, and the bourgeoisie. National Assembly French Revolutionary assembly (1789-1791). Called first as the Estates General, the three estates came together and demanded radical change. It passed the Declaration of the Rights of Man in 1789. The Storming of the Bastille 14 July 1789, start of the French Revolution and national holiday for France, was a political prison where weapons and political enemies of the king were locked up, <cover>symbol of the Old Regime and the King's oppression Execution of Louis XVI 1793. King was killed due to his monarchial views on ruling France, which all of the citizens greatly disagreed with The reign of terror 40,000 people killed for going against revolution and Robespierre </cover>was behind it. The engine of the Terror was the guillotine.\" , \"start_char\": 686.000000 , \"title\": \"Napoleon Flashcards | Quizlet\" , \"url\": \"https://quizlet.com/54280907/napoleon-flash-cards/\" }"}}
