{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre \"louis must die that the country may live\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_23_775302119#0_1715663332","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2627","rank":1,"snippet":"Report... Any law which violates the inalienable rights of man is essentially unjust and tyrannical; it is not a law at all. Maximilien Robespierre Source Report... The general will rules in society as the private will governs each separate individual. Maximilien Robespierre Source Report... The secret of freedom lies in educating people, whereas the secret of tyranny is in keeping them ignorant. Maximilien Robespierre Source Report... Any institution which does not suppose the people good, and the magistrate corruptible, is evil. Maximilien Robespierre Source Report... It is with regret that I pronounce the fatal truth: <cover>Louis must die that the country may live. Maximilien Robespierre</cover>Source Report... Lf the attribute of popular government in peace is virtue, the attribute of popular government in revolution is at one and the same time virtue and terror, virtue without which terror is fatal, terror without which virtue is impotent. The terror is nothing but justice, prompt, severe, inflexible; it is thus an emanation of virtue.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Maximilien Robespierre (20+ Sourced Quotes) - Lib Quotes\" , \"url\": \"https://libquotes.com/maximilien-robespierre\" }"}}
