{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre \"death of louis xvi\" republic)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_795239265#10_1402239863","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2634","rank":1,"snippet":"\"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_07_795239265#10_1402239863\" , \"end_char\": 6244.000000 , \"headings\": \"A brief history of France. A brief history of France. The Ancient History of France The Franks place in the History of France - Country of the Franks<cover>Robespierre & the Reign of Terror in the history of France Napoleon Bonaparte in the History of France \" , \"segment\": \"In 1792 France declared war on Austria. Louis XVI was apprehended in his attempt to flee France, and executed soon after. In 1793 France declared war on Great Britain. A French Constitution was adopted but not put into effect. The new Republic's motto read \\\"Freedom, Equality, Fraternity\\\", and the people patriotically stood behind it. After the death of Louis XVI </cover>in 1793, the Reign of Terror made its ugly debut. The first victim in the carnage was Marie Antoinette who had been imprisoned with her children after being seperated from Louis. Her son, Louis Charles, (Louis XVII), had mysteriously disappeared just before her execution, (guillotine-style). Soon there followed a long line of unfortunate French citizens to their "}}
