{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ robespierre louis death necessary)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_172107280#0_346116927","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2636","rank":1,"snippet":"be put to death because of an opinion about society? Subpar conditions in France caused Maximilien <cover>Robespierre, the leader of the radical phase of the French Revolution, to enact the “Reign of Terror”, which was an extremely violent response to the reign of Louis XVI by the revolutionary government. During this period of two years, the Guillotine, or “National Razor” dropped a heavy blade on the necks of thousands of people who were unjustly tried and condemned to death. The actions of the revolutionary government during the Reign of Terror in France were not justified. The internal and external threats that France was facing at the time did not warrant the brutal and violent methodology …show more content… Not only did this attack on christianity betray the ideals that would have made it justified, but it also caused an undermining of an entire religion that many people followed. Finally, in October 1793, revolutionaries destroyed 1600 homes and chopped off 12 heads in 5 minutes in Lyons (Doc C). This shows once again how the violence used was to a much greater degree than necessary. </cover>Thus, The internal threats during the Reign of Terror did not justify the horrible actions of "}}
